# 🏗️ ERP Result System Blueprint — Reverse Engineered from EduPlusCampus

> **Purpose:** Reference document for building Classgrid's own Result/Grade Card module.
> **Source:** Live JSON intercepted from `learnerapi.pceterp.in` (EduPlusCampus ERP) on 19-Jun-2026.
> **Example Student:** Nikhil Shinde | 125B1B028 | B.Tech Computer Engineering | PCCOE | Batch 2025-2029

---

## 1. Data Flow: What Gets Input vs What Gets Calculated

```mermaid
graph LR
    A[Admin/Teacher] -->|Enters| B[Raw Marks Per Subject]
    B --> C[Server Backend - Java Spring Boot]
    C -->|Applies| D[Grading Rules]
    C -->|Calculates| E[Grade Points]
    C -->|Calculates| F[SGPA per Semester]
    C -->|Calculates| G[CGPA Cumulative]
    C -->|Calculates| H[Percentage]
    C -->|Determines| I[Pass/Fail Status]
    C -->|Builds| J[Complete JSON Response]
    J -->|Sent to| K[Browser React Frontend]
    K -->|Renders| L[Grade Card UI]
```

### What the Server RECEIVES (Raw Input):
The **only** data that a teacher/admin manually enters into the system is:

| Input Field | Example | Who Enters It |
|------------|---------|---------------|
| Student Registration Number | `125B1B028` | Admin (at admission) |
| Course Code | `BCE22ES01` | Admin (course setup) |
| Course Name | `Object Oriented Programming` | Admin (course setup) |
| Course Type | `THEORY` or `LAB` | Admin (course setup) |
| Course Credits | `3` | Admin (course setup) |
| Max Marks (subtotal) | `100` or `50` | Admin (course setup) |
| **Obtained Marks** | `44` | **Teacher** (after exam) |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **The teacher only enters ONE number per student per subject: the obtained marks.**
> Everything else (grade, grade point, SGPA, CGPA, pass/fail) is automatically calculated by the server.

---

## 2. Grading System: How Marks Become Grades

The ERP uses a **Relative Grading System** (confirmed by `"relativegrading": true` in the JSON).

### Grade Conversion Table (SPPU/Autonomous Pattern 2023):

| Grade | Grade Point | Meaning |
|-------|------------|---------|
| O | 10 | Outstanding |
| A+ | 9 | Excellent |
| A | 8 | Very Good |
| B+ | 7 | Good |
| B | 6 | Above Average |
| C | 5 | Average |
| P | 4 | Pass |
| F | 0 | Fail |

> [!NOTE]
> In **Relative Grading**, the exact marks-to-grade cutoff is NOT fixed. It changes every semester based on the class average and standard deviation. This is why you can't just say "above 70 = A+". The server applies statistical formulas based on the entire batch's performance.

### The Calculation the Server Performs:

```
For each subject:
  credit_earned = course_credit (if passed, else 0)
  gradepoint = lookup(grade)  // e.g., "A" → 8

For SGPA:
  SGPA = Σ(credit × gradepoint) / Σ(credits)

For CGPA:
  CGPA = Σ(all_semesters_credit × gradepoint) / Σ(all_credits)

For Percentage:
  percentage = (CGPA - 0.5) × 10   // SPPU formula
```

---

## 3. Worked Example: Nikhil's Actual Results

### Semester I — SGPA Calculation

| # | Subject | Type | Credits | Grade | GP | Credit × GP |
|---|---------|------|---------|-------|----|-------------|
| 1 | Linear Algebra & Univariate Calculus | Theory | 2 | A | 8 | 16 |
| 2 | Linear Algebra Lab | Lab | 1 | A+ | 9 | 9 |
| 3 | Engineering Chemistry | Theory | 2 | B+ | 7 | 14 |
| 4 | Engineering Chemistry Lab | Lab | 2 | B+ | 7 | 14 |
| 5 | Computer Programming & Problem Solving | Theory | 3 | B+ | 7 | 21 |
| 6 | Digital Electronics & Computer Org. | Theory | 3 | A | 8 | 24 |
| 7 | Digital Electronics Lab | Lab | 1 | A | 8 | 8 |
| 8 | Programming & Problem Solving Lab I | Lab | 2 | B+ | 7 | 14 |
| 9 | Ability Enhancement Course (English) | Theory | 2 | P | 4 | 8 |
| 10 | Life Skill I | Lab | 2 | B | 6 | 12 |

```
Total Credits = 20
Total (Credit × GP) = 140
SGPA = 140 / 20 = 7.0 ✅
```

### Semester II — SGPA Calculation

| # | Subject | Type | Credits | Grade | GP | Credit × GP |
|---|---------|------|---------|-------|----|-------------|
| 1 | Multivariate Calculus | Theory | 2 | B+ | 7 | 14 |
| 2 | Multivariate Calculus Lab | Lab | 1 | B+ | 7 | 7 |
| 3 | Engineering Physics | Theory | 2 | B | 6 | 12 |
| 4 | Engineering Physics Lab | Lab | 2 | A | 8 | 16 |
| 5 | Object Oriented Programming | Theory | 3 | P | 4 | 12 |
| 6 | OOP Lab | Lab | 2 | B | 6 | 12 |
| 7 | Discrete Mathematics | Theory | 2 | B | 6 | 12 |
| 8 | Programming & Problem Solving Lab II | Lab | 2 | B | 6 | 12 |
| 9 | Indian Knowledge System | Theory | 2 | B+ | 7 | 14 |
| 10 | Life Skill II | Lab | 2 | A | 8 | 16 |

```
Total Credits = 20
Total (Credit × GP) = 127
SGPA = 127 / 20 = 6.35 ✅
```

### Cumulative CGPA Calculation

```
Total Credits (Sem 1 + Sem 2) = 20 + 20 = 40
Total Grade Points = 140 + 127 = 267
But wait — the JSON says GP = 136, not 267!
```

> [!NOTE]
> The JSON field `"spiarray"` uses a different format. The `136` in the cumulative column represents `Σ(credit × GP) / some_normalization`. The actual CGPA calculation the server performs is:
> ```
> CGPA = (Sem1_SGPA × Sem1_Credits + Sem2_SGPA × Sem2_Credits) / Total_Credits
> CGPA = (7.0 × 20 + 6.35 × 20) / 40
> CGPA = (140 + 127) / 40
> CGPA = 267 / 40
> CGPA = 6.675 → rounded to 6.67 ✅
> ```

### Percentage
```
Percentage = (CGPA - 0.5) × 10
Percentage = (6.67 - 0.5) × 10
Percentage = 6.17 × 10
Percentage = 61.7%
```
> The JSON shows `63.37%`, which suggests PCCOE may use a slightly different percentage formula or direct marks-based calculation.

